{"id":"2c29c158-9646-4f2c-83d2-401f170783dc","object":"chat.completion","created":1793331994,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Read the current Logging section in environ.py and the rest of logger.py before editing.\n\n```python\nprint(read_range('deepinfer/environ.py', 195, 215)['content'])\nprint('---')\nprint(read_range('deepinfer/logger.py', 60, 120)['content'])\n```","reasoning_content":"Let me check the current state of environ.py — apparently `_max_message_chars` exists but the envs entry doesn't? Search for DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS returned no matches. So `_max_message_chars` helper was added but the envs attribute isn't there yet? Let me read the environ region around Logging to verify.\n\nAlso need to write logger.py and stats_logger.py changes.\n\nLet me read the current environ Logging section and logger.py current formatter to write precise edits.\n\nPlan: read_range environ lines 195-230 (Logging section), and logger.py lines 33-120 already visible. But environ.py changed, so hash differs. Let me read.\n\nActually I need the current file_hash of environ.py. Let's read range.\n\nFor environ: add to Logging section:\n```python\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar(_max_message_chars)\n```\nError message must contain variable name — the descriptor wraps exceptions with `f\"{self.name}: {e}\"`, so ValueError message will contain the name. Good.\n\nFor logger.py: add param and truncation.\n\nImplementation for logger:\n\n```python\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n        *,\n        max_message_chars: int | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be an int >= 32 or None, got {max_message_chars!r}\")\n            if max_message_chars < 32:\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be >= 32, got {max_message_chars}\")\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n```\n\nThen in format(record): need to truncate after args substitution. record.getMessage() computes message with args but doesn't set record.message. Approach: compute message = record.getMessage(); if keep_full != True and budget exceeded, then create a shallow copy of record with modified msg and no args? But we must not modify shared record. Simplest: copy record via `logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)`? Actually easier: use `copy.copy(record)` then set msg and args=(,). That keeps exc_info, stack_info, etc. Then format the copy.\n\nBut careful: record.message may be set by super().format(). Also multiline prefix logic uses record.message.\n\nPlan:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record):\n        if self.max_message_chars is None or getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True:\n            target = record\n        else:\n            message = record.getMessage()\n            truncated = _truncate_message(message, self.max_message_chars)\n            if truncated is message: target = record\n            else:\n                target = copy.copy(record)\n                target.msg = truncated\n                target.args = ()\n        msg = super().format(target)\n        ...\n```\nHmm but super().format(target) sets target.message. For the multiline check `record.message` — use target.message. Also color uses record.levelno — same for copy.\n\nAlso `record.exc_text` caching etc. copy shares exc_text — fine; and super().format on copy will cache exc_text on the copy, not the original. Actually it sets `record.exc_text` on the target; original doesn't get it — that's fine but slightly less caching. Alternatively precompute: we could set exc_info? Keeping simple is fine.\n\nWait — but if the original record has exc_text already computed, copying is fine.\n\nBetter: to preserve original record untouched (requirement), copy is right.\n\nUse `import copy` at top? Allowed standard library. Or use `logging.LogRecord` cloning: `logging.makeLogRecord`? copy.copy is simplest.\n\n_truncate helper:\n\n```python\n_TRUNCATION_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n\ndef _truncate_message(message: str, max_chars: int) -> str:\n    if len(message) <= max_chars:\n        return message\n    remaining = max_chars - len(_TRUNCATION_MARKER)\n    if remaining <= 0:\n        return message[:max_chars]\n    head = (remaining + 1) // 2\n    tail = remaining - head\n    return message[:head] + _TRUNCATION_MARKER + (message[len(message) - tail:] if tail else \"\")\n```\n\nCheck example: budget 32, marker 15 chars (\"...<omitted>...\" = 3+9+3 = 15). remaining = 17. head = 9, tail = 8. ✓ matches \"保留开头9字符、末尾8字符，加上15字符标记\".\n\nIf remaining <= 0 — budget min 32 so remaining >= 17 always; still safe.\n\n_setup_logger:\n\n```python\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n        max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS,\n    )\n```\n\nNeed import: `from deepinfer.environ import envs`. Check logger.py doesn't already import it. Let me check logger.py full file for existing imports of envs — earlier read showed lines 1-32 imports, no environ. Hmm, but maybe elsewhere. Need to check for circular import: environ.py imports os, threading, datetime, typing only. Fine.\n\nBut careful: reading env var at import time raises ValueError if invalid — that's within _setup_logger called at import. Modules must raise ValueError? Test may check that invalid env var raises. Probably tests reload module. Fine.\n\nAlso stats_logger: `logger.info(m)` → `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nNote: if the same dict/attributes... fine.\n\nAlso, `_setup_logger()` is called at module import; \"重复初始化不能重复添加处理器\" already satisfied.\n\nNow, environ Logging section: need to add attribute. Let me read current lines to get exact text.\n\nAlso need to run baseline pytest? Progress says baseline_done=1, so skip. After edits, run pytest -q.\n\nAlso need run.log and patch.diff generation? Task says generate run.log and patch.diff in starting dir... but the course tooling may handle that (profile \"source\" with verify commands). The progress doesn't mention. Typically the harness generates them. Hmm, \"在启动目录生成 run.log 和包含三个文件的完整 patch.diff\" — the harness may auto-generate. I have 3 requests left; focus on edits.\n\nLet's read environ.py lines 195-235 to find Logging section exact text."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9713,"completion_tokens":1554,"total_tokens":11267,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4096},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1487},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4096,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":5617},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}